      "message": "fix(post): each mill post carries a flipped WCS axis and an inverted machine axis\n\nThe engine mirrors a section with a flipped WCS X or Y (#1649) and a\nprogram for a machine with an inverted X or Y (#374). Only fanuc.cps and\nhaas.cps declared `axisInversion = true`, so each other mill script\nrefused the two cases by name.\n\nMazak, Doosan DNM, Siemens 840D, Heidenhain, Mach4, grblHAL, Tormach,\nTinyG, Carvera and LinuxCNC now declare the flag. Each writes the\nsection note `WCS X FLIPPED - PROGRAM MIRRORED` and the header note\n`MACHINE X+ MOVES LEFT - INVERTED AXIS` in its comment form.\n\nThe proof is crates/post/tests/wcs_flip_dialects.rs with the new reader\ntests/mirror_trace. The reader reads each posted program as a controller\nwhose X, Y, or X and Y run reversed. It compares the physical cut runs\nwith the CAM path point by point, the physical compensation side, and\nthe rapid end points. It reads native arcs, split arcs, chords, R-word\narcs, a helix, G81, the Heidenhain G200 / M99 call and expanded holes.\nThe standard program on the reversed controller must stray.\n\nProbing stays refused: in a flipped WCS (engine), and on an inverted\nmachine axis through the ten scripts (no probeAxisInversion).\n\nThe refusal hint \"(Fanuc, Haas)\" is now \"(each built-in mill post\ndoes)\". The refusal tests use a lathe script and a mill script with the\nflag removed.\n\nFixes #2475\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
